        "id": 5633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T22:31:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The more math-y methods that have their own namespace can use a lower_case_with_underscores convention (like skvx::), and there\u0027s also sk_bit_cast, sk_malloc, etc. Since these are math formulas more than procedures I personally prefer the lower case names. Would you consider letting having us leave it? I like the look of \"wangs_formula::cubic_log2\" better than \"wangs_formula::CubicLog2\".\n\nI put it in a skgpu::tess::wangs_formula namespace because code outside of here does use nextlog16. I\u0027m tempted to just do \"::wangs_formula\" at global scope though (not skgpu::tess::wangs_formula). Thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "b298c231_918a6e59",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 62
