      "writtenOn": "2021-10-14T13:57:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, mathy functions as lower_case_with_underscores is a good counter example, so I\u0027ll withdraw that request 😊\n\nI also prefer ::wangs_formula to skgpu::tess::wangs_formula. I\u0027d be okay with skgpu::wangs_formula as well since it\u0027s probably only used by the GPU backend, but the default path renderer, aa linearizing path renderer, and triangulating path renderer all use Wang\u0027s formula. That\u0027s why it had originally been moved out of the v1/tess work and into geom/\n\nIf we\u0027re making src/gpu/tessellate be something independent of v1 and more represent math and types that just know how to tessellate and/or triangulate curves, then I think having WangsFormula.h there is okay. But like your change to remove skgpu::geom namespace from the types in experimental/graphite/src/geom, having ::tess:: part of the namespace probably doesn\u0027t give us much.",
